  "lineage": "Uyghur On Ikki Muqam (\"Twelve Muqams\") classical Central Asian art-music tradition of the Uyghur Turkic-Muslim population of the Tarim Basin (Xinjiang). UNESCO Masterpiece 2005, Representative List 2008. The twelve canonical muqamat — Rak, Chebbiyat, Mushavrek, Charigah, Pengigah, Ozhal, Echeh, Ushshaq, Bayat, Nava, Sigah, Iraq — each comprises three sections: chong naghma free-rhythm great-song suite; dastan metrically-bound narrative-song; faster mashrap social-dance section. Turdi Akhun in the 1950s codified recensions; the Xinjiang Muqam Ensemble anchors institutional transmission.",
